      "at": "2026-08-15T04:33:23Z",
      "excerpt": "Yeah, `rx.el.input(type=\"hidden\")` works fine, so if it were just \"how do I render a hidden input\" then a docs line would cover it. What #6874 runs into is that `rx.input(type=\"hidden\")` accepts the prop and still renders a visible bar, because the Radix wrapper keeps its height regardless of the input inside it. So less discoverability, more that this one takes a standard prop and quietly does the wrong thing with it. That said, I'm not attached to this approach. If you'd rather just document i"
